<title>AUSTRALIA: RUGBY UNION-AUCKLAND BEAT NEW SOUTH WALES 34-20.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-AUCKLAND BEAT NEW SOUTH WALES 34-20.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Auckland beat New South Wales 34-20 (halftime 13-20) in a Super 12 rugby union match at the Sydney Football Stadium on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Auckland - Tries: Zinzan Brooke, Brian Lima (2), Dylan Mika. Conversions: Adrian Cashmore (4). Penalties: Adrian Cashmore (2).</p>
<p>New South Wales - Tries: Alistair Murdoch (2). Conversions: Matthew Burke (2). Penalties: Matthew Burke (2).</p>
</text>
